  "instructions": [
    "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Cook the spaghetti for 9 to 10 minutes until tender, then drain.",
    "Pat the chicken dry. Mix the flour, salt, and pepper on a plate and coat each cutlet, shaking off extra.",
    "Heat the oil and 1 tbsp butter in a 12 inch skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the cutlets 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden and 165 F inside, working in two batches if needed.",
    "Move the chicken to a plate and cover it with foil.",
    "Lower the heat to medium. Add the garlic to the skillet and stir for 30 seconds.",
    "Pour in the broth and lemon juice. Scrape up the browned bits and simmer 4 to 5 minutes until reduced by about a third.",
    "Stir in the capers and the remaining 3 tbsp butter until the sauce is smooth.",
    "Return the chicken and any juices to the pan and spoon sauce over it for 1 minute.",
    "Toss the spaghetti with some of the sauce. Serve topped with the chicken, more sauce, and parsley."
  ],
